**Mission**: give Node.js CLI authors a single, dependency-free, strict-by-default framework that turns a declarative command description into parsing + validation + help + process behavior, without ever leaking its own opinions into the user's dependency tree.

**Users**: every Node CLI author — from one-off scripts (the global `program` singleton) to large multi-command CLIs (local `new Command()`), including TypeScript users via hand-maintained typings and the separate `@commander-js/extra-typings` project.

**Evidence of reach**: >10M weekly downloads ([dev.to audit of >10M/week packages](https://dev.to/piiiico/i-audited-every-npm-package-with-10m-weekly-downloads-here-is-the-risk-map-16k0)); dependabot traffic shows GitLab, Keycloak, bitwarden, Zendesk, Automattic/juice on commander (C36).

## 2. Architecture Map

**Runtime shape** (all sizes measured at snapshot):

```
index.js (24 ln)   CJS entry: exports program singleton, create* factories, 6 classes
esm.mjs (16 ln)    ESM wrapper: named re-exports from CJS
lib/command.js (2777 ln)   Command extends EventEmitter — orchestrator
lib/option.js  (380 ln)    Option model + flags-string parser + DualOptions helper
lib/argument.js (150 ln)   Argument model
lib/help.js    (747 ln)    Help class — help-text rendering pipeline
lib/error.js    (39 ln)    CommanderError, InvalidArgumentError
lib/suggestSimilar.js (100 ln)  Damerau–Levenshtein "did you mean" suggestions
typings/        index.d.ts (1113 ln, hand-maintained) + esm.d.mts re-export + tsd tests
tests/          109 jest files, feature-organized (options.*, command.*, help.*, …)
examples/       44 runnable examples incl. executable-subcommand CLIs
docs/           terminology, deprecated, release-policy, help-in-depth, options-in-depth, parsing-and-hooks + zh-CN translations
```

**Parse pipeline** (documented in docs/parsing-and-hooks.md; implemented in command.js):

1. `parse()`/`parseAsync()` → `_prepareForParse()` (save/restore state for repeat parses, C12) → `_prepareUserArgs()` (argv conventions: node/electron/eval/user auto-detection, C20)
2. `_parseCommand()` → `parseOptions()` — the tokenizer: a hand-rolled state machine (`activeGroup` for combined shorts, `activeVariadicOption`, `--` literal handling, negative-number heuristics, positional/passThrough modes) that classifies each token as known option / operand / unknown
3. Values dispatched via **EventEmitter** events (`option:name`, `optionEnv:name`) → `handleOptionValue` → `setOptionValueWithSource` (value + provenance: default/config/env/cli/implied)
4. Env vars → implied values → subcommand dispatch (`_dispatchSubcommand`, `preSubcommand` hooks) → leaf: help check → mandatory/conflict/unknown checks → `_processArguments` → `preAction` hooks → action handler → `postAction` hooks (promise-chained so `parseAsync` works)
5. Errors funnel through `this.error()` → `_outputConfiguration.outputError` → `_exit()` (process.exit unless `exitOverride`)

**Help pipeline**: `helpInformation()` → `createHelp()` (new Help + configureHelp overrides) → `formatHelp()` — grouping (v14 help groups), wrapping (`boxWrap`, `formatItem`), style hooks (identity by default; color via `configureOutput`/`configureHelp`).

**Executable subcommands** (C13): `.command(name, desc)` marks `_executableHandler`; at dispatch, `_executeSubCommand` searches the script directory (with legacy name fallback), spawns a child (node for source files, incl. `.ts`/`.mjs`), forwards signals, increments `--inspect` ports, and terminates the parent with the child's exit code.

## 3. Critical Components

| Component | Lines | Role | Why critical |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Command.parseOptions` | command.js:1748-1895 | Tokenizer/classifier | The heart of the library; every parsing special case (negative numbers, `--`, combined shorts, variadic greediness, positional/passThrough) lives here. Highest regression risk (C24). |
| `Command._parseCommand` | command.js:1550-1641 | Dispatch/validation orchestrator | Orders help checks, mandatory/conflict checks, action invocation; subtle ordering choices (e.g., "We do not always call this check to avoid masking a 'better' error") |
| `Command.addOption` + event handlers | command.js:670-733 | Value semantics | Defaults, negate defaults, presets, parseArg, value sources; the `option:` events are simultaneously the internal dispatch bus and a documented public API (C11) |
| `Command._executeSubCommand` | command.js:1202-1346 | Child-process management | Process-spawning surface; signal forwarding; exit coupling to parent |
| `Help` class | help.js:1-747 | Help rendering | Second-largest module; hand-rolled wrapping/grouping/colors |
| `Option.splitOptionFlags` | option.js:328-377 | Flags-string grammar | v13 made this strict (throws on `-ws`); the flags DSL is the library's public grammar |
| `typings/index.d.ts` | 1113 lines | TS surface | Hand-maintained; the only verified defect (C26) lives here |
| Test suite | 109 files | Safety net | Mitigates the parser's complexity; the reason the conservative change process works |

## 4. Design Decisions

| # | Decision | Rationale / tradeoff | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| D1 | **Zero production dependencies** | Supply-chain safety + tiny install; cost: parsing/help/color/suggestion logic all hand-rolled | CONTRIBUTING.md:40 |
| D2 | **Strict by default** (unknown options, unknown commands, and since v13 excess args are errors) with opt-outs (`allowUnknownOption`, `allowExcessArguments`) | Catches user mistakes; opt-outs keep escape hatches | CHANGELOG.md:82; Readme.md:73 |
| D3 | **EventEmitter as internal dispatch bus AND public legacy API** | `option:name` / `command:name` events predate modern APIs and remain documented; coupling is deliberate for backward compat | command.js:720, 1608; Readme.md:956-964 |
| D4 | **Major version ~every 6 months, tied to Node LTS EOL; 12-month security window for old majors** | Predictable support story; forces periodic Node-floor bumps | docs/release-policy.md |
| D5 | **Backward compatibility as a first-class constraint** — 9+ documented deprecated features still supported (RegExp parseArg since v3, `_args` since v11, string-form `addHelpCommand`, …) | Zero-drama upgrades for a >10M-download audience; cost: growing API surface constraining evolution | docs/deprecated.md |
| D6 | **Option value provenance tracking** (`default/config/env/cli/implied`) | Enables `env()`, `implies()`, `conflicts()`, and correct precedence without magic | command.js:39, 953-992 |
| D7 | **Hand-maintained typings + JSDoc + `tsc --checkJs` + tsd** instead of codegen | Single source of implementation truth; typings checked but hand-synced (drift mechanism proven by C26) | package.json:25-27; tsconfig.json |
| D8 | **Lazy creation of help option/help command** | Cheap defaults; help only materialized when needed | command.js:463, 2592 |
| D9 | **Output/exit configurability** (`configureOutput`, `exitOverride`) | Lets tests and embedding apps (Electron, daemons) own stdout/exit | Readme.md:1110-1152 |
| D10 | **Save/restore state for repeat `parse()`** (v13) | Test-friendly, REPL-friendly; explicitly forbidden under `storeOptionsAsProperties` | command.js:1127-1174 |
| D11 | **Executable subcommands as first-class citizens** | Unix-style `prog-sub` discovery, node-launched on Windows, inspector port bumping | command.js:1202-1346 |
| D12 | **`program` singleton export + `new Command()` guidance** | Convenience for scripts; docs steer larger apps to instances | index.js:7; Readme.md:147-175 |

